# Pathway Tools 27.0 (/opt/pathway-tools/aic-export/pathway-tools/ptools/27.0). The tag
# is a name, not a published tag: the installer is licensed, so the image is never pulled.
# A host supplies it as a local SIF in the agent home's container store, under the name
# this URI maps to (docker..quay.io_txyliu_pathologic..27.0.sif). On fir that SIF is
# /scratch/phyberos/mp4/private/pathologic.sif, sha256
# 86fd8d9cfb7d45d0207a556d7c976f4b58664b1bd0420e2b7e69315b9dcfd514, built 2026-06-05
# from quay.io/txyliu/pathologic:latest (pinned 2026-10-21). A different image under this
# name is a different Pathway Tools, and nothing downstream will notice; check the digest.
#
# The repository is not anonymously pullable (a manifest request returned 401 on
# 2026-09-05), and `txyliu/` is a personal namespace, so a host without the SIF cannot
# stage this step.
#
# It carries no `conda:` line, so under the MAMBA runtime the staging preflight refuses it
# by name -- correctly: there is no form of this step a container-less agent can run.
container: docker://quay.io/txyliu/pathologic:27.0
